# ABB EQ meters B23 (direct, 65 A) and B24 (CT connected) with RS485, protocol set to Modbus.
# Addresses are exactly as sent on the bus. Readable range is 0x1000-0x8EFF; any block of 1-125 registers works.
# Quantities a model does not have read as "invalid": all FFFF for unsigned, the largest positive value for signed.
# Basic (steel) variants, B23/B24 1xx-xxx, only have import registers.
# The manual does not state the factory RS485 settings; check them on the meter display.
@mbmap=1
@vendor=ABB
@model=B23 / B24
@vendor_website=abb.com
@description=Three-phase DIN rail energy meters of the EQ B-series (B23 direct connected, B24 CT connected), Modbus RTU over RS485
@source=ABB, "B23/B24 User Manual", 2CMC485003M0201 revision E (2025-11-07); https://library.abb.com/d/2CMC485003M0201
@protocol=rtu
@unit_id=1
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@max_read_registers=125
@sentinel_uint16=0xFFFF=Invalid
@sentinel_int16=0x7FFF=Invalid
@sentinel_uint32=0xFFFFFFFF=Invalid
@sentinel_int32=0x7FFFFFFF=Invalid
@sentinel_uint64=0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF=Invalid
@sentinel_int64=0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFF=Invalid

